@page "/dashboard/mentor"
@layout AppLayout
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = Roles.Mentor + "," + Roles.Admin + "," + Roles.Staff)]
@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Mentor
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Components
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Services
@using AuthWithAdmin.Shared.AuthSharedModels
@inject IMentorWorkspaceService Workspace
@inject IPersonalTasksService PersonalTasks
@inject IRoadmapStagesService Roadmap
@inject NavigationManager Nav

@*
    ── בית — the mentor's daily cross-project workspace ─────────────────────
    Visual source:  design/design-system/Motiva Mentor Dashboard.dc.html —
                    the finished Mentor dashboard, and the file this screen is
                    now transcribed from. It supersedes Motiva Mentor Home.dc.html
                    for this route: same four questions, a different composition.
    Data source:    IMentorWorkspaceService. Everything about "what is waiting
                    on me" — which items, how long they have waited, how urgent
                    that is and in what order — comes from
                    GET /api/mentor/attention. This page does not filter by
                    status, compute an age or compare against a threshold; the
                    daily digest reads the very same model, which is what keeps
                    the morning email and this screen in agreement.

    THE COMPOSITION IS THE DESIGN'S, THE CONTENT IS THE PRODUCT'S
    The reference's own order and proportions:

        greeting + workload line          (38px / 15px, baseline-aligned)
        two shortcut pills
        ┌ main column                1.75fr ─────┬ בקרוב            1fr ─┐
        │ ┌ דורש את תשומת לבך — the bright card ┐ │  4 dated entries      │
        │ └─────────────────────────────────────┘ │  + ליומן המלא          │
        │ ┌ הצוותים שלי — the quiet card ───────┐ │                       │
        │ └─────────────────────────────────────┘ │                       │
        └─────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────┘

    Its people (רונית, צוות אוריון/נובה/אטלס), its counts and its dates are
    prototype data and none of it is copied. Every row here is a real
    MentorAttentionItemDto, MentorProjectSummaryDto or MentorCalendarEvent.

    ── FOUR SECTIONS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    The reference draws three. משימות אישיות is the fourth and it is required
    on this dashboard, so it is BUILT FROM THE FILE'S OWN PARTS rather than
    designed: the file's quiet card, the file's quiet head, the file's row,
    and המשימות שלי's existing 19px round checkbox. Nothing about it is a new
    visual idea, and it introduces no new endpoint — _ws.PersonalTasks is
    already in the snapshot this page loads, and the checkbox calls the same
    IPersonalTasksService.ToggleAsync the tasks screen calls.

    It sits under בקרוב because both are narrow quiet lists, and because that
    is what brings the side column's height up to the main column beside it.

    ── A COMMAND CENTRE, NOT THREE TABLES ───────────────────────────────────
    The page answers three questions and is sized to be answered in seconds:
    what needs me now, how are my teams, what is next. Each list is therefore
    a SHORTLIST — 4 attention groups, 5 teams, 4 dated entries, 5 tasks — and
    each row carries the fewest facts that still identify it:

        attention   bar · team / what is waiting · how long · chevron
        team        dot · name · stage · note
        בקרוב        when · what it is · whose
        task        checkbox · title · when it is due

    What each row lost is not lost from the product: the item's milestone is
    on the screen the row opens, and the team's progress bar is on
    /mentor/projects/{id}. The counts — the heading badge and the two shortcut
    pills — still come from the server, so the shortlists never hide a number.

    ── משימות אישיות APPEARS TWICE, AND THAT IS CORRECT ─────────────────────
    The card lists the mentor's reminders. The attention section may ALSO show
    a משימות אישיות group — but only for the ones that are actually waiting
    (overdue, or due today), because that section is "what is blocked on me"
    and the card is "my list". A task that is simply next appears only on the
    card; a task that is late appears on both, once as a queue item and once
    as a line to tick off.

    ── THE THREE-UP HEALTH GRID (מצב הפרויקטים) IS GONE ─────────────────────
    The reference has no health tiles: it carries health as a per-team dot and
    note in הצוותים שלי, which is the same fact stated once per team instead of
    three times in aggregate. The three tiles were also navigation — each
    opened פרויקטים בהנחייתי filtered to that state via MentorLinks.Projects(state).
    That helper, those routes and the filter on the projects page are ALL
    untouched and still work; what is gone is this page's shortcut to them.

    ── THE REFERENCE'S ATTENTION DETAIL IS THE DRAWER, NOT A ROW PER ITEM ───
    The file draws one row per ITEM. This screen groups them by team and opens
    the team's real items in a drawer, because MentorAttentionItemDto carries
    title, project, team, milestone, actor, waiting age and href and nothing
    else — a row-per-item list padded out to the reference's copy would be
    exactly the static design content this pass is not allowed to introduce.
    The navigation contract is unchanged: every row inside the drawer still
    opens THAT item's own screen, with its id in the URL.
*@

<div class="mh-page">

    @* ── Title ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       The greeting alone. The reference's title row carries no second
       line — the workload sentence that used to sit on its baseline is
       gone, and the two shortcut pills under it state the same counts
       the sentence did. *@
    <header class="mh-title-row">
        <h1 class="mh-greeting">@Greeting</h1>
    </header>

    @if (_loading)
    {
        <div class="mh-state" role="status" aria-live="polite">
            <span class="mh-spinner" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span>טוענת את סביבת העבודה…</span>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        @* ── Shortcut pills ───────────────────────────────────────────
           Real counts from the attention model, each opening the queue
           that owns it. A pill whose count is zero is not rendered. *@
        @if (Counts.AwaitingRequests > 0 || Counts.PendingSubmissions > 0)
        {
            <div class="mh-shortcuts">
                @if (Counts.AwaitingRequests > 0)
                {
                    <a class="mh-shortcut" href="@MentorLinks.Requests">
                        <span class="mh-shortcut-dot mh-dot-violet" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        @(Counts.AwaitingRequests == 1
                            ? "בקשה אחת ממתינה לך"
                            : $"{Counts.AwaitingRequests} בקשות ממתינות לך")
                    </a>
                }
                @if (Counts.PendingSubmissions > 0)
                {
                    <a class="mh-shortcut" href="@MentorLinks.Reviews">
                        <span class="mh-shortcut-dot mh-dot-blue" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        @(Counts.PendingSubmissions == 1
                            ? "הגשה אחת לבדיקה"
                            : $"{Counts.PendingSubmissions} הגשות לבדיקה")
                    </a>
                }
            </div>
        }

        @* ── ROW 1 — דורש את תשומת לבך (1.75fr) · בקרוב (1fr) ────────── *@
        <div class="mh-row mh-row-1">

            @* ── 1. דורש את תשומת לבך ──────────────────────────────
               The page's one lifted card, and the only one wearing the
               reference's three-hue glow. Rows are teams; the items
               inside open IN PLACE. *@
            <div class="mh-col">
                <section class="mh-card mh-card-primary" aria-labelledby="mh-attn-h">
                    <div class="mh-card-head">
                        <h2 class="mh-card-title mh-card-title-lg" id="mh-attn-h">דורש את תשומת לבך</h2>
                        @if (Counts.Total > 0)
                        {
                            <span class="mh-count"
                                  aria-label="@($"{Counts.Total} פריטים דורשים את תשומת לבך")">@Counts.Total</span>
                        }
                        <a class="mh-card-link" href="@MentorLinks.Tasks">לכל הפריטים</a>
                    </div>

                    @if (_attention.Count == 0)
                    {
                        <p class="mh-calm">
                            <strong>הכול תחת שליטה.</strong>
                            אין הגשות, בקשות או משימות שדורשות את תשומת לבך כרגע.
                        </p>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <div class="mh-attn-list">
                            @foreach (var group in _attention)
                            {
                                var g    = group;
                                var open = _openGroup == g.Key;

                                <div class="mh-attn-group">
                                    <button type="button"
                                            class="mh-attn-row"
                                            @onclick="@(() => ToggleGroup(g.Key))"
                                            aria-expanded="@open"
                                            aria-controls="@($"mh-g-{g.Key}")"
                                            aria-label="@($"{g.Name} — {g.Summary}")">
                                        <MStatusBar Tone="@g.Tone" />

                                        <span class="mh-attn-body">
                                            <span class="mh-attn-name">@g.Name</span>
                                            <span class="mh-attn-summary">@g.Summary</span>
                                        </span>

                                        <span class="@(g.IsEscalated ? "mh-attn-time mh-attn-time-late" : "mh-attn-time")">@g.Urgency</span>

                                        <span class="@(open ? "mh-chevron mh-chevron-open" : "mh-chevron")" aria-hidden="true">
                                            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                                                 stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                                                <path d="M15 6l-6 6 6 6"></path>
                                            </svg>
                                        </span>
                                    </button>

                                    @* The group expands IN PLACE, as the reference draws
                                       it, and so does the item inside it: a row opens its
                                       own popup OVER this dashboard rather than navigating
                                       to the screen that owns it. Each popup carries the
                                       CTA that does the navigating — see OpenAttentionItem. *@
                                    @if (open)
                                    {
                                        <div class="mh-attn-items" id="@($"mh-g-{g.Key}")">
                                            @foreach (var item in g.Items)
                                            {
                                                var it = item;
                                                <button type="button" class="mh-attn-item"
                                                        @onclick="@(() => OpenAttentionItem(it))"
                                                        aria-label="@($"פתיחת {it.Title}")">
                                                    <MStatusBadge Variant="@MentorAttentionRows.TypeVariant(it)"
                                                                  Text="@MentorAttentionRows.TypeLabel(it)" />
                                                    <span class="mh-attn-item-title" title="@it.Title">@it.Title</span>
                                                    <span class="@(MentorAttentionRows.IsEscalated(it) ? "mh-attn-item-time mh-attn-time-late" : "mh-attn-item-time")">
                                                        @MentorAttentionRows.TimeLabel(it)
                                                    </span>
                                                </button>
                                            }
                                        </div>
                                    }
                                </div>
                            }
                        </div>
                    }
                </section>
            </div>

            @* ── 2. בקרוב ──────────────────────────────────────────
               A 46px date block per entry, its kind carried as an inset
               top bar in the calendar's own five hues. *@
            <section class="mh-card mh-card-quiet" aria-labelledby="mh-up-h">
                <div class="mh-card-head">
                    <span class="mh-head-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                             stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="18" rx="3"></rect>
                            <path d="M16 2v4M8 2v4M3 10h18"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="mh-card-title" id="mh-up-h">בקרוב</h2>
                    <a class="mh-card-link mh-card-link-sm" href="@MentorLinks.Calendar">ליומן המלא</a>
                </div>

                @if (_upcomingLoading)
                {
                    <div class="mh-substate">
                        <span class="mh-spinner-sm" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span>טוענת אירועים…</span>
                    </div>
                }
                else if (_upcoming.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="mh-empty">אין אירועים קרובים ביומן.</p>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="mh-up-list">
                        @foreach (var e in _upcoming)
                        {
                            var ev = e;
                            <button type="button" class="mh-up-row"
                                    @onclick="@(() => OpenEvent(ev))"
                                    aria-label="@($"פתיחת {ev.Title}")">
                                <span class="@($"mh-up-tile mh-kind-{MentorEventTypes.CssSuffix(e.Type)}")">
                                    <span class="mh-up-day">@e.Date.Day.ToString("00")</span>
                                    <span class="mh-up-month">@MotivaDates.ShortMonth(e.Date)</span>
                                </span>
                                <span class="mh-up-body">
                                    <span class="mh-up-title" title="@e.Title">@e.Title</span>
                                    <span class="mh-up-meta">@UpcomingRelative(e) · @UpcomingContext(e)</span>
                                </span>
                            </button>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
            </section>
        </div>

        @* ── ROW 2 — משימות אישיות (1fr) · הצוותים שבהנחייתי (1.75fr) ──
           The reference's checkerboard: the wide card sits on the
           reading side in row 1 and on the far side in row 2, so the two
           rows do not stack into one column of the same width. *@
        <div class="mh-row mh-row-2">

            @* ── 4. משימות אישיות ──────────────────────────────────
               The mentor's own reminders, off the snapshot the page has
               already loaded. The checkbox calls the same
               IPersonalTasksService.ToggleAsync המשימות שלי calls and
               flips locally, so ticking one never costs a page load. *@
            <section class="mh-card mh-card-quiet mh-tasks" aria-labelledby="mh-tasks-h">
                <div class="mh-card-head">
                    <span class="mh-head-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                             stroke-width="2.1" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="mh-card-title" id="mh-tasks-h">משימות אישיות</h2>
                    <a class="mh-card-link mh-card-link-sm" href="@MentorLinks.PersonalTasks">לכל המשימות</a>
                </div>

                @if (_tasks.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="mh-empty">אין משימות אישיות כרגע.</p>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="mh-task-list">
                        @foreach (var task in _tasks)
                        {
                            var t  = task;
                            var id = t.Id;
                            <div class="mh-task-row">
                                <button type="button"
                                        class="@(t.IsDone ? "mh-check mh-check-on" : "mh-check")"
                                        role="checkbox"
                                        aria-checked="@t.IsDone"
                                        aria-label="@($"סימון \"{t.Title}\" כהושלמה")"
                                        disabled="@(_togglingId == id)"
                                        @onclick="@(() => ToggleTaskAsync(id))">
                                    @if (t.IsDone)
                                    {
                                        <svg width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                                             stroke-width="3.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                                            <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"></path>
                                        </svg>
                                    }
                                </button>

                                <button type="button"
                                        class="@(t.IsDone ? "mh-task-title mh-task-title-done" : "mh-task-title")"
                                        @onclick="@(() => OpenTask(t))" title="@t.Title">@t.Title</button>

                                <span class="@TaskDueClass(t)">@TaskDue(t)</span>
                            </div>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
            </section>

            @* ── 3. הצוותים שבהנחייתי ──────────────────────────────
               Every supervised team, worst-first, four deep — see
               ShortlistTeams for why this no longer excludes the teams
               that are also in דורש את תשומת לבך. *@
            <section class="mh-card mh-card-quiet" aria-labelledby="mh-teams-h">
                <div class="mh-card-head">
                    <span class="mh-head-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                             stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                            <path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"></path>
                            <circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"></circle>
                            <path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"></path>
                        </svg>
                    </span>
                    <h2 class="mh-card-title" id="mh-teams-h">הצוותים שבהנחייתי</h2>
                    <a class="mh-card-link" href="@MentorLinks.Projects()">לכל הצוותים</a>
                </div>

                @if (_teams.Count == 0)
                {
                    <p class="mh-empty">לא משויכים אליך פרויקטים כרגע.</p>
                }
                else
                {
                    <div class="mh-team-list">
                        @foreach (var t in _teams)
                        {
                            var team = TeamRow(t);
                            <button type="button" class="mh-team-row"
                                    @onclick="@(() => OpenProject(t.Id))"
                                    aria-label="@($"פתיחת פרטי {team.Name}")">
                                <span class="mh-team-id">
                                    <span class="@($"mh-team-dot mh-tone-{team.Tone}")" role="img"
                                          aria-label="@team.Label"></span>
                                    <span class="mh-team-text">
                                        <span class="mh-team-name" title="@team.Name">@team.Name</span>
                                        <span class="mh-team-stage">
                                            אבן דרך נוכחית: <span class="mh-team-stage-val" title="@team.Stage">@team.Stage</span>
                                        </span>
                                    </span>
                                </span>
                                <span class="@($"mh-team-note mh-tone-{team.Tone}")" title="@team.Note">@team.Note</span>
                            </button>
                        }
                    </div>
                }
            </section>
        </div>

        @* ── The colour key ───────────────────────────────────────────
           One quiet line under the dashboard, and the only thing on this
           screen that explains rather than reports.

           IT EXISTS FOR בקרוב. Every other colour on the page sits beside
           the words that mean it — a team's pill says "באיחור 224 ימים"
           in its own tone, an attention bar sits next to the summary that
           explains it. The date tiles are the exception: their kind is a
           2.5px bar and nothing on the row names it.

           So the key lists the CALENDAR's five kinds, and it reads them
           from MentorEventTypes — the same Ordered list, the same Label
           and the same CssSuffix the tiles themselves use. Nothing here
           declares a colour or invents a meaning; a kind renamed or
           recoloured for the calendar changes here in the same commit. *@
        <div class="mh-legend" role="group" aria-label="מקרא צבעים ביומן">
            @foreach (var kind in MentorEventTypes.Ordered)
            {
                <span class="mh-legend-item">
                    <span class="@($"mh-legend-dot mh-kind-{MentorEventTypes.CssSuffix(kind)}")"
                          aria-hidden="true"></span>@MentorEventTypes.Label(kind)
                </span>
            }
        </div>
    }
</div>

@*  ── Inspection popups, all opened OVER this dashboard ────────────────────
    The rule this screen now follows: clicking an entity on an overview
    INSPECTS it here; only the CTA inside the popup navigates. None of these
    is a page-local implementation — the Quick View is the same panel
    פרויקטים בהנחייתי opens, the request modal is the same one המשימות שלי
    opens, and the task editor is the same one יומן ותכנון opens. *@
<MentorProjectQuickView Card="@_openProject"
                        Focus="@_openProjectFocus"
                        OnClose="CloseProject" />

<MentorRequestModal RequestId="@_openRequestId"
                    WaitingLabel="@OpenRequestWaitingLabel"
                    OnClose="@(() => _openRequestId = null)"
                    OnChanged="ReloadAsync" />

<MentorPersonalTaskModal IsOpen="@(_openTask is not null)"
                         EditingTask="@_openTask"
                         Projects="@_ws.Projects"
                         OnClose="@(() => _openTask = null)"
                         OnSaved="@(_ => TaskChangedAsync())"
                         OnDeleted="@(_ => TaskChangedAsync())" />

@code {
    [CascadingParameter] private User? _user { get; set; }

    private MentorWorkspace _ws = MentorWorkspace.Empty;
    private bool _loading = true;

    /// <summary>Everything waiting on this mentor, GROUPED BY TEAM and left
    /// in the server's own worst-first order. See BuildAttentionTeams.</summary>
    private IReadOnlyList<MentorAttentionTeam> _attention = Array.Empty<MentorAttentionTeam>();

    /// <summary>The supervised teams that are NOT in the section above — see
    /// QuietTeams.</summary>
    private List<MentorProjectSummaryDto> _teams    = new();
    private List<MentorCalendarEvent>     _upcoming = new();

    /// <summary>משימות אישיות — the mentor's own reminders, open ones first.
    /// Straight off the snapshot the page already loaded; the card issues no
    /// request of its own.</summary>
    private List<PersonalTaskDto> _tasks = new();

    /// <summary>The task whose checkbox is mid-flight, so it cannot be clicked
    /// twice. Same guard המשימות שלי uses.</summary>
    private int? _togglingId;

    /// <summary>The key of the expanded attention group, or null. The
    /// reference opens a group IN PLACE under its own row rather than in a
    /// dialog, and only one at a time — clicking a second closes the first,
    /// which is what keeps the card's height from running away.</summary>
    private string? _openGroup;

    /// <summary>בקרוב fills in after the rest of the screen. See LoadUpcomingAsync.</summary>
    private bool _upcomingLoading = true;

    // ── Inspection state ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // WHY THESE ARE FIELDS AND NOT ROUTES. Every one of them used to be an
    // href: a team row went to /mentor/projects/{id}, a submission to that
    // route with ?submissionId=, a request to /mentor-requests?requestId= and
    // a personal task to /mentor/tasks?editTask=. Each of those navigations
    // then opened a popup on ARRIVAL, so one click cost the mentor the screen
    // they were reading in order to show them a panel that could just as well
    // have opened here. Clicking an entity on an overview is INSPECTION, and
    // inspection does not move you. The destinations are all still reachable —
    // each popup carries the CTA that goes there, and that CTA is now the only
    // thing on this screen that changes the URL.

    /// <summary>The project whose Quick View is open, or null.</summary>
    private MentorProjectCard? _openProject;

    /// <summary>The attention row the mentor clicked, when the Quick View was
    /// opened from one. It decides which submission the panel names and where
    /// its primary CTA goes, so clicking the second of two waiting submissions
    /// does not offer the first.</summary>
    private MentorAttentionItemDto? _openProjectFocus;

    private int?             _openRequestId;
    private PersonalTaskDto? _openTask;

    /// <summary>Roadmap progress per project, for the Quick View's stage line.
    ///
    /// <para>Loaded in the BACKGROUND, exactly like בקרוב and for the same
    /// reason: this dashboard paints from one fast snapshot, and holding it
    /// behind a second round-trip to fill in one line of a panel that is not
    /// open yet would be paying for it on every visit. Absent, the card falls
    /// back to the project summary's own milestone — the same degradation
    /// פרויקטים בהנחייתי takes when a cycle has no stages configured.</para></summary>
    private IReadOnlyDictionary<int, ProjectRoadmapProgressDto> _roadmap =
        new Dictionary<int, ProjectRoadmapProgressDto>();

    /// <summary>Waiting phrase for the request currently open, taken from the
    /// same attention item the row rendered — so the modal and the row it was
    /// opened from cannot word one request two ways.</summary>
    private string? OpenRequestWaitingLabel =>
        _openRequestId is int id
            ? _ws.AwaitingMe.FirstOrDefault(r => r.EntityId == id)?.WaitingLabel
            : null;

    /// <summary>
    /// How many rows each list shows — a SHORTLIST, not a window onto the
    /// whole queue.
    ///
    /// <para>The attention cap counts TEAMS now, not items, which is why four
    /// is generous rather than tight: four teams can carry a dozen items
    /// between them and the drawer reaches every one. The list arrives
    /// worst-first from the server and the grouping preserves that order, so
    /// the top four teams ARE the four that matter; "לכל הפריטים" is the way
    /// to the rest. Nothing is lost, only deferred one click.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>בקרוב shows four, which is what the dashboard reference draws and
    /// what the rail's own height beside a two-card column will hold.</para></summary>
    private const int AttentionRows = 4;
    private const int TeamRows      = 4;
    private const int TaskRows      = 4;
    private const int UpcomingRows  = 3;

    /// <summary>Server-computed counts. The workload sentence, the shortcut
    /// pills and the section badge all read these rather than counting a list,
    /// so they cannot disagree with each other or with the daily digest.</summary>
    private MentorAttentionCountsDto Counts => _ws.Attention.Counts;

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() => await ReloadAsync();

    private async Task ReloadAsync()
    {
        _loading = true;
        _ws = await Workspace.LoadAsync();

        // Already filtered, aged and ordered worst-first by the server. No
        // .Where on status and no .OrderBy on a timestamp — grouping preserves
        // that order rather than replacing it.
        _attention = BuildAttentionTeams(_ws.Attention.Items).Take(AttentionRows).ToList();
        _teams     = ShortlistTeams();
        _tasks     = ShortlistTasks(_ws.PersonalTasks);
        _openGroup = null;

        _loading = false;

        // NOT awaited, and deliberately so. BuildCalendarAsync issues one
        // GetProjectDetailAsync per project on top of the snapshot — it is what
        // makes /mentor/calendar take the better part of ten seconds on a full
        // caseload. Awaiting it here would hold the ENTIRE screen behind the
        // one block that needs it, so Home paints from the single fast snapshot
        // and בקרוב fills itself in a moment later.
        _ = LoadUpcomingAsync();
        _ = LoadRoadmapAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>Roadmap progress, off the critical path. Same contract as
    /// LoadUpcomingAsync: it fills a detail in, it never gates the paint, and a
    /// failure leaves the fallback wording rather than an error.</summary>
    private async Task LoadRoadmapAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            var entries = await Roadmap.GetMentorProjectsProgressAsync()
                          ?? new List<MentorRoadmapEntryDto>();

            _roadmap = entries.GroupBy(e => e.ProjectId)
                              .ToDictionary(g => g.Key, g => g.First().Progress);
        }
        catch
        {
            _roadmap = new Dictionary<int, ProjectRoadmapProgressDto>();
        }
    }

    // ── Opening an entity, in place ─────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>Opens one project's Quick View over this dashboard.</summary>
    private void OpenProject(int projectId, MentorAttentionItemDto? focus = null)
    {
        var project = _ws.Projects.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Id == projectId);

        // A project the snapshot does not carry cannot be summarised honestly,
        // so fall back to the route rather than opening an empty panel.
        if (project is null)
        {
            Nav.NavigateTo(focus?.Href ?? $"/mentor/projects/{projectId}");
            return;
        }

        _openProjectFocus = focus;
        _openProject      = MentorProjectCard.Build(_ws, project, _roadmap.GetValueOrDefault(projectId));
    }

    private void CloseProject()
    {
        _openProject      = null;
        _openProjectFocus = null;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// One attention row, opened in the popup that owns its kind.
    ///
    /// <para>A request opens the request modal and a personal task opens its
    /// editor — both the shared components, both already the in-place behaviour
    /// on המשימות שלי. A submission opens the project's Quick View FOCUSED on
    /// it: the mentor sees which submission is waiting and how long it has
    /// waited without leaving the dashboard, and the panel's primary CTA is
    /// that submission's own review screen. There is no shared review popup to
    /// mount here — the review drawer belongs to מרחב הפרויקט — and inventing a
    /// second one is exactly the duplication this pass is avoiding.</para></summary>
    private void OpenAttentionItem(MentorAttentionItemDto item)
    {
        switch (item.Kind)
        {
            case MentorAttentionKind.Request:
                _openRequestId = item.EntityId;
                break;

            case MentorAttentionKind.PersonalTask:
                OpenTask(_ws.PersonalTasks.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == item.EntityId));
                break;

            default:
                if (item.ProjectId is int pid) OpenProject(pid, item);
                else Nav.NavigateTo(item.Href);
                break;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// One בקרוב row, opened in place like everything else on this screen.
    ///
    /// <para>The three kinds this list carries used to be three different
    /// navigations: a personal task or a meeting went to /mentor/tasks?editTask=
    /// and opened its editor there, a review went to the project route with
    /// ?submissionId= and opened the drawer there, and a milestone or a dated
    /// deliverable went to the project workspace. Two of the three were the
    /// navigate-then-popup pattern; all three now open the panel here and offer
    /// the same destination as a CTA.</para></summary>
    private void OpenEvent(MentorCalendarEvent e)
    {
        switch (e.Type)
        {
            case MentorEventType.PersonalTask:
            case MentorEventType.Meeting:
                OpenTask(_ws.PersonalTasks.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == e.EntityId));
                break;

            case MentorEventType.Review when e.ProjectId is int reviewPid:
                OpenProject(reviewPid, _ws.Reviews.FirstOrDefault(r => r.EntityId == e.EntityId));
                break;

            // A milestone or a dated deliverable is not an entity a mentor
            // opens — it is a date ON a project, so the project is what the
            // panel shows.
            default:
                if (e.ProjectId is int pid) OpenProject(pid);
                else                        Nav.NavigateTo(e.Href ?? MentorLinks.Calendar);
                break;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The shared personal-task editor. Null — a task the snapshot no
    /// longer carries — falls back to המשימות שלי rather than opening the
    /// editor on nothing.</summary>
    private void OpenTask(PersonalTaskDto? task)
    {
        if (task is null) Nav.NavigateTo(MentorLinks.PersonalTasks);
        else              _openTask = task;
    }

    /// <summary>A save or a delete closes the editor and re-reads the snapshot,
    /// so the attention count, the group summaries and the task list all move
    /// together rather than one of them going stale.</summary>
    private async Task TaskChangedAsync()
    {
        _openTask = null;
        await ReloadAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>בקרוב, from the same builder /mentor/calendar renders — so a
    /// meeting reads identically in both places. Filtered to what is still
    /// ahead: an undated entry cannot be "coming up", and a past one is not
    /// either.</summary>
    private async Task LoadUpcomingAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            var today = DateTime.Today;
            var events = await Workspace.BuildCalendarAsync(_ws);

            _upcoming = events
                .Where(e => e.Date.Date >= today)
                .OrderBy(e => e.Date)
                .Take(UpcomingRows)
                .ToList();
        }
        catch
        {
            // A failed calendar build empties one card; it must not take the
            // screen down with it. The empty state below says so honestly.
            _upcoming = new();
        }
        finally
        {
            _upcomingLoading = false;
            await InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
        }
    }

    // ── Copy ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private string Greeting
    {
        get
        {
            var name = _user?.FirstName?.Trim();
            var hour = DateTime.Now.Hour;

            // Written as conditionals rather than as a `switch { < 12 => … }`
            // relational pattern on purpose: inside a .razor @code block the
            // Razor parser reads a leading `<` as the start of a tag and the
            // whole code block stops compiling.
            var part = hour < 12 ? "בוקר טוב"
                     : hour < 17 ? "צהריים טובים"
                     : hour < 21 ? "ערב טוב"
                     :             "לילה טוב";

            return string.IsNullOrEmpty(name) ? part : $"{part}, {name}";
        }
    }

    // TodayLine — the "5 צוותים בליווי · 3 פריטים ממתינים" sentence that used
    // to sit on the greeting's baseline — is gone with the reference's own
    // title row, which now carries the greeting and nothing else. Both of its
    // numbers survive on the screen: the workload is the two shortcut pills
    // and the attention card's count, and the team count is the length of
    // הצוותים שבהנחייתי.

    // ── דורש את תשומת לבך ───────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // ONE ROW PER TEAM, not one row per item, and that is the whole point of
    // this pass. A mentor's decision on this screen is "which team do I open
    // now" — three rows for one team is that decision asked three times, and
    // it also meant a single noisy team could fill the shortlist and hide
    // every other team that was waiting.
    //
    // The row states four things, in the lecturer home's own order: a colour
    // bar for how serious it is, the team, a "·"-joined summary of WHAT is
    // waiting, and how long the worst of it has waited. The items themselves
    // are one click away in the drawer.

    /// <summary>
    /// Everything one team is waiting on, as a single row.
    ///
    /// <para><paramref name="Items"/> keeps the server's worst-first order, so
    /// the drawer lists them in the same order the queue would.</para></summary>
    private sealed record MentorAttentionTeam(
        int? ProjectId,
        /// <summary>Stable id for the accordion. The project id, or "personal"
        /// for the mentor's own group — which is why this is a string: that
        /// group genuinely has no project.</summary>
        string Key,
        string Name,
        string Context,
        string Summary,
        string Urgency,
        bool IsEscalated,
        MStatusBar.BarTone Tone,
        IReadOnlyList<MentorAttentionItemDto> Items);

    /// <summary>
    /// Groups the attention list by project, WITHOUT re-sorting it.
    ///
    /// <para>Group order is first-appearance order in the server's list, which
    /// is already worst-first — so the team holding the single most pressing
    /// item is the first row, exactly as it was when rows were items. Nothing
    /// here computes an age, a threshold or a priority.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Items with no project (the mentor's own reminders) are a real
    /// group of their own rather than being dropped: they are things waiting on
    /// this mentor, they simply have no team. They sort by the same rule as
    /// every other group.</para></summary>
    private static List<MentorAttentionTeam> BuildAttentionTeams(
        IReadOnlyList<MentorAttentionItemDto> items)
    {
        // A list of buckets rather than a Dictionary, because the key is int?
        // and the personal group's key is genuinely null — which a Dictionary
        // will not accept. The scan is over a handful of projects.
        var buckets = new List<(int? Id, List<MentorAttentionItemDto> Items)>();

        foreach (var i in items)
        {
            var slot = buckets.FindIndex(b => b.Id == i.ProjectId);
            if (slot < 0)
            {
                buckets.Add((i.ProjectId, new List<MentorAttentionItemDto> { i }));
                continue;
            }
            buckets[slot].Items.Add(i);
        }

        return buckets.Select(b =>
        {
            var worst = b.Items[0];   // the list is worst-first, so the head IS the worst

            return new MentorAttentionTeam(
                ProjectId:    b.Id,
                Key:          b.Id?.ToString() ?? "personal",
                // NOT "המשימות שלי" — that is the name of a nav item, and a row
                // that borrows it reads as a link to that screen.
                Name:         b.Id is null ? "משימות אישיות" : MentorAttentionRows.Team(worst),
                Context:      GroupContext(b.Id, b.Items),
                Summary:      GroupSummary(b.Items),
                Urgency:      MentorAttentionRows.TimeLabel(worst),
                IsEscalated:  MentorAttentionRows.IsEscalated(worst),
                Tone:         GroupTone(b.Items),
                Items:        b.Items);
        }).ToList();
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The row's summary — "בקשה ממתינה · משימה באיחור · הגשה לבדיקה".
    ///
    /// <para>One phrase per KIND present, counted, in the order those kinds
    /// first appear in the group's own worst-first list. So the phrase a mentor
    /// reads first is the phrase for the item the server considered most
    /// pressing, and the sentence cannot re-order itself between renders.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>A personal task is the one kind that may read as באיחור, because it
    /// is the one kind with a deadline. A submission or a request has a waiting
    /// age and no deadline to be late for — the same rule
    /// <see cref="MentorAttentionRows.TimeLabel"/> enforces.</para></summary>
    private static string GroupSummary(IReadOnlyList<MentorAttentionItemDto> items)
    {
        var phrases = new List<string>(3);

        foreach (var kind in items.Select(i => i.Kind).Distinct())
        {
            var of = items.Where(i => i.Kind == kind).ToList();
            var n  = of.Count;

            phrases.Add(kind switch
            {
                MentorAttentionKind.Submission => n == 1 ? "הגשה לבדיקה"  : $"{n} הגשות לבדיקה",
                MentorAttentionKind.Request    => n == 1 ? "בקשה ממתינה"  : $"{n} בקשות ממתינות",

                // Overdue is stated only when it is true of at least one of
                // them; a task that is merely due is not late.
                MentorAttentionKind.PersonalTask when of.Any(i => i.IsOverdue)
                                               => n == 1 ? "משימה באיחור" : $"{n} משימות באיחור",
                MentorAttentionKind.PersonalTask
                                               => n == 1 ? "משימה לביצוע" : $"{n} משימות לביצוע",
                _                              => n == 1 ? "פריט ממתין"   : $"{n} פריטים ממתינים",
            });
        }

        return string.Join(" · ", phrases);
    }

    /// <summary>The drawer's sub-title: the project behind the team name, plus
    /// the milestone when every waiting item sits under the same one. Two
    /// different milestones and it says nothing rather than picking one.</summary>
    private static string GroupContext(int? projectId, IReadOnlyList<MentorAttentionItemDto> items)
    {
        if (projectId is null) return "פריטים אישיים — ללא שיוך לצוות";

        var parts = new List<string>(2);

        var project = items.Select(i => i.ProjectTitle).FirstOrDefault(t => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(t));
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(project)) parts.Add(project!);

        var stages = items.Select(i => i.MilestoneTitle)
                          .Where(m => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(m))
                          .Distinct()
                          .ToList();
        if (stages.Count == 1) parts.Add(stages[0]!);

        return string.Join(" · ", parts);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The leading colour bar — the row's seriousness at a glance.
    ///
    /// <para>Rose the moment ANY item in the group has escalated, because that
    /// is the fact a mentor is scanning for; blue — the finished palette's
    /// "in progress / waiting" role — otherwise. Two hues, not a type marker:
    /// the chips inside the group say what kind each item is. המשימות שלי maps
    /// the same model onto the same two tones, so one item cannot be rose on
    /// one screen and violet on the other. This never decides what "escalated"
    /// means — <c>MentorAttentionAge</c> arrives already set by
    /// GET /api/mentor/attention.</para></summary>
    private static MStatusBar.BarTone GroupTone(IReadOnlyList<MentorAttentionItemDto> items) =>
        items.Any(MentorAttentionRows.IsEscalated)
            ? MStatusBar.BarTone.Rose
            : MStatusBar.BarTone.Blue;

    /// <summary>Expand a group, or collapse it if it is already the open one.
    /// One at a time, as the reference does it.</summary>
    private void ToggleGroup(string key) => _openGroup = _openGroup == key ? null : key;


    // ── הצוותים שלי — the quiet half ────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Every supervised team, worst-first, four deep.
    ///
    /// <para><b>It no longer excludes the teams that are also in דורש את תשומת
    /// לבך.</b> The previous pass filtered them out so a team could never be
    /// named twice on one screen. The reference does not: its own list carries
    /// צוות Motiva and צוות הספרייה הדיגיטלית while both are sitting in the
    /// attention card above, and its note pill has a tone for exactly that
    /// state ("הגשה ממתינה לבדיקה") which no team could ever reach under the
    /// filter. The two cards are answering different questions — WHAT IS
    /// BLOCKED ON ME versus HOW ARE MY TEAMS — and the same team legitimately
    /// appears in both answers.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Order is the shared signal priority, then the nearest deadline —
    /// the same ordering פרויקטים בהנחייתי uses, so the top of this list is the
    /// top of that screen.</para></summary>
    private List<MentorProjectSummaryDto> ShortlistTeams() =>
        _ws.Projects
           .OrderBy(p => MentorProjectSignals.Priority(SignalOf(p)))
           .ThenBy(p => p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate ?? DateTime.MaxValue)
           .Take(TeamRows)
           .ToList();

    /// <summary>One team row.
    ///
    /// <para><paramref name="Tone"/> is one of the reference's FOUR keys —
    /// alert · request · wait · ok — not MStatusDot's three. The file gives
    /// each of them a dot hue, an ink and a pill wash, and "הגשה ממתינה
    /// לבדיקה" (wait) is a state the three-tone triad has nowhere to put. It
    /// is a plain string because it names a CSS modifier, and because
    /// MStatusDot must not gain a fourth member to serve one screen.</para></summary>
    private sealed record TeamOverviewRow(
        string Name, string Stage, string Note, string Label, string Tone);

    /// <summary>
    /// The project's signal, from the three real columns.
    ///
    /// <para><b>Why this is not Projects.HealthStatus.</b> That column is never
    /// written by this application, so in practice every project comes back
    /// OnTrack and the row would draw a calm dot beside a milestone that is
    /// visibly overdue. The state is read off real columns instead, through the
    /// shared <see cref="MentorProjectSignal"/> — the same vocabulary
    /// פרויקטים בהנחייתי filters and colours its rows with, so one team cannot
    /// read one way here and another way there.
    /// <see cref="MentorHealthStates"/> is untouched and still owns the health
    /// column for the day it starts being written.</para></summary>
    private MentorProjectSignal SignalOf(MentorProjectSummaryDto p) =>
        MentorProjectSignals.Of(
            milestoneOverdue: MentorTime.IsOverdue(p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate),
            pendingReviews:   p.PendingMentorReview,
            openRequests:     _ws.OpenRequestsFor(p.Id));

    /// <summary>
    /// One team row: a dot, the name over its current milestone, and the
    /// state as a filled pill at the row's end.
    ///
    /// <para>The pill IS the reference's treatment here — it moved from the
    /// bright card to this one when the attention rows stopped carrying
    /// chips. The dot keeps the state as an accessible name, so the colour is
    /// never the only carrier of it.</para></summary>
    private TeamOverviewRow TeamRow(MentorProjectSummaryDto p)
    {
        var signal = SignalOf(p);

        return new TeamOverviewRow(
            Name:   TeamLabel(p),
            Stage:  string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.CurrentMilestoneTitle)
                        ? "טרם החל" : p.CurrentMilestoneTitle!,
            Note:   TeamNote(signal, p),
            Label:  MentorProjectSignals.Label(signal),
            Tone:   TeamTone(signal));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The state pill's text.
    ///
    /// <para>MentorProjectSignals.Note stays the single source for every
    /// signal's wording; a late project just loses its "אבן דרך " prefix here.
    /// The row already names the milestone one line above — "אבן דרך נוכחית:
    /// ניתוח" — so the pill repeating the words is the same fact stated twice
    /// in the space of two lines, and what a reader actually needs from the
    /// pill is the ONE thing the line above does not say: how late it is.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Local to this screen, like TaskDue: פרויקטים בהנחייתי draws the
    /// same note WITHOUT a milestone line beside it, so there the prefix is
    /// still carrying its weight.</para></summary>
    private string TeamNote(MentorProjectSignal signal, MentorProjectSummaryDto p)
    {
        var note = MentorProjectSignals.Note(
            signal, p.CurrentMilestoneDueDate,
            p.PendingMentorReview, _ws.OpenRequestList(p.Id));

        return signal == MentorProjectSignal.Late && note.StartsWith("אבן דרך ", StringComparison.Ordinal)
            ? note["אבן דרך ".Length..]
            : note;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The four tones, mapped one-to-one onto the four signals this product
    /// already computes — so the pill's colour is not a second opinion about
    /// the team, it is the same signal פרויקטים בהנחייתי filters by.
    ///
    /// <para>alert = a missed deadline · wait = a submission queued on the
    /// mentor · request = someone else may still be holding it · ok = nothing
    /// waiting.</para></summary>
    private static string TeamTone(MentorProjectSignal s) => s switch
    {
        MentorProjectSignal.Late       => "alert",
        MentorProjectSignal.Submission => "wait",
        MentorProjectSignal.Request    => "request",
        _                              => "ok",
    };

    /// <summary>What the row is called. The reference names every row with a
    /// team ("צוות אוריון"), but TeamName is optional in this schema and the
    /// seed carries projects with none — an unnamed row is unclickable in
    /// practice, so it falls back to the project's own title.</summary>
    private static string TeamLabel(MentorProjectSummaryDto p) =>
        string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(p.TeamName) ? p.Title : p.TeamName;


    // ── בקרוב ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // The dashboard reference's rail: a coloured when-cell and a title, four
    // dated entries deep, closed by a link to the full calendar.

    /// <summary>The team the entry belongs to. A mentor's own reminder has
    /// none, and says so rather than printing a blank line.</summary>
    private static string UpcomingContext(MentorCalendarEvent e)
    {
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(e.TeamName))     return e.TeamName;
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(e.ProjectTitle)) return e.ProjectTitle;
        return "תזכורת אישית";
    }

    // ── The date block ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // A 46px tile — day over month — with the entry's KIND carried as an
    // inset top bar, in the same five hues Motiva Mentor Calendar uses. The
    // file's own comment says so: "semantic colors mirror Motiva Mentor
    // Calendar KIND map". The tile itself never changes colour; only the
    // 2.5px bar across its top does, so a column of tiles stays a column of
    // dates rather than becoming a column of chips.
    //
    // Under the title, "how soon · whose" in one 12.5px line — the file's
    // `{{ e.rel }} · {{ e.team }}`.

    /// <summary>
    /// How far off it is, in words — "היום", "מחר", "בעוד 5 ימים".
    ///
    /// <para>The hour rides along when there IS one.
    /// <c>MentorCalendarEvent.HasTime</c> is true for exactly one thing — a
    /// mentor personal task whose owner filled in שעת התחלה — so a real slot
    /// is never dropped and one is never invented.</para></summary>
    private static string UpcomingRelative(MentorCalendarEvent e)
    {
        var days = (e.Date.Date - DateTime.Today).Days;

        var when = days switch
        {
            0 => "היום",
            1 => "מחר",
            2 => "בעוד יומיים",
            _ => $"בעוד {days} ימים",
        };

        return e.HasTime ? $"{when} · {e.Date:HH:mm}" : when;
    }


    // ── משימות אישיות ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // The mentor's own reminders, as a card rather than as a row inside
    // דורש את תשומת לבך. The two are not the same statement: the attention
    // model carries the tasks that are WAITING — overdue, or due today — and
    // this card is the list itself, including the ones that are simply next.
    // A mentor ticking something off on the dashboard is the reason it has a
    // checkbox instead of a chevron.

    /// <summary>Overdue count, for the heading's annotation. Personal tasks are
    /// the one kind on this screen with a real DueDate, so באיחור is a true
    /// statement about them and about nothing else here — the same rule
    /// המשימות שלי follows.</summary>
    private int PersonalOverdue =>
        _ws.PersonalTasks.Count(t => !t.IsDone && MentorTime.IsOverdue(t.DueDate));

    /// <summary>
    /// The card's shortlist: open tasks first, soonest deadline first, undated
    /// last, and completed ones only if there is room left.
    ///
    /// <para>Done tasks are not filtered out entirely. A task ticked off on
    /// this card must not vanish from under the pointer that ticked it — the
    /// struck-through row IS the confirmation — so they sort to the back
    /// instead.</para></summary>
    private static List<PersonalTaskDto> ShortlistTasks(IReadOnlyList<PersonalTaskDto> all) =>
        all.OrderBy(t => t.IsDone)
           .ThenBy(t => t.DueDate ?? DateTime.MaxValue)
           .Take(TaskRows)
           .ToList();

    /// <summary>
    /// Tick / untick, against the same endpoint המשימות שלי calls.
    ///
    /// <para>The row flips locally rather than reloading the workspace: the
    /// toggle answers a bool, and re-running the snapshot to learn one bit
    /// would make a checkbox feel like a page load. The list is NOT re-sorted
    /// afterwards, so the row a mentor just ticked stays where they ticked
    /// it.</para></summary>
    /// <summary>
    /// The due pill's text — "מחר", "בעוד 4 ימים", "באיחור 3 ימים".
    ///
    /// <para>MentorTime.DeadlineLabel is still the source, so a task's deadline
    /// is computed once for the whole product; this only drops its "יעד "
    /// prefix. In a pill that is ALREADY the row's deadline column the word is
    /// a label for the column, not information about the task, and the two
    /// dated arms are the only ones that carry it — "בעוד 4 ימים" and
    /// "באיחור 3 ימים" never did. Stripping it is what makes the column read
    /// as one series instead of two.</para>
    ///
    /// <para>Local to this screen ON PURPOSE. המשימות שלי draws the same label
    /// in a wide Meta cell where "יעד היום" is a sentence rather than a chip,
    /// and MentorProjectsPage reads it too, so the shared helper is left
    /// exactly as it was.</para></summary>
    private static string TaskDue(PersonalTaskDto t)
    {
        var label = MentorTime.DeadlineLabel(t.DueDate);
        if (label is null) return "";

        return label.StartsWith("יעד ", StringComparison.Ordinal)
            ? label["יעד ".Length..]
            : label;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Its three washes, as the reference draws them: grey once the task is
    /// done, rose while it is late, blue otherwise.
    ///
    /// <para>Done wins over late, deliberately — a completed task is not
    /// still overdue, and leaving it rose would keep alarming about work that
    /// is finished.</para></summary>
    private static string TaskDueClass(PersonalTaskDto t) =>
        string.IsNullOrEmpty(TaskDue(t))         ? "mh-task-due mh-task-due-none"
        : t.IsDone                                ? "mh-task-due mh-task-due-done"
        : MentorTime.IsOverdue(t.DueDate)         ? "mh-task-due mh-task-due-late"
        :                                           "mh-task-due";

    private async Task ToggleTaskAsync(int id)
    {
        _togglingId = id;
        var ok = await PersonalTasks.ToggleAsync(id);
        _togglingId = null;

        if (!ok) return;

        var hit = _tasks.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == id);
        if (hit is not null) hit.IsDone = !hit.IsDone;

        // The snapshot's own copy, so the heading's overdue count and the
        // attention model's view of this task cannot disagree with the row.
        var source = _ws.PersonalTasks.FirstOrDefault(t => t.Id == id);
        if (source is not null && !ReferenceEquals(source, hit)) source.IsDone = !source.IsDone;
    }
}
